**Day 45: Flask – Connecting to MySQL**  

**Topic:**  
Connecting a Flask application to a MySQL database using the `mysql-connector-python` library. Executing queries from Flask and fetching/displaying data in a web page.  

**Learning Objectives:**  

• Understand how to integrate Flask with MySQL.  
• Learn to execute SQL queries from a Flask application.  
• Fetch and display database records in a web interface.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  

• Set up a Flask app with MySQL connectivity.  
• Write and execute SQL queries to retrieve employee data.  
• Display the fetched employee list on a webpage.  

**Important Concepts:**  

• Database connection pooling in Flask.  
• Secure handling of database credentials.  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  

• `SELECT * FROM employees;`  
• `cursor.execute(query)`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  

• Building internal dashboards for employee management.  
• Displaying dynamic data from a database on a company website.  

**Tools / Tech:**  

• Flask  
• mysql-connector-python  
• MySQL  

**Summary:**  
Learned how to connect a Flask application to a MySQL database, execute queries, and display results on a webpage. This is essential for building dynamic web applications that interact with databases.  

